<title>SWEDEN: Frontline buys tanker fleet.</title>
<headline>Frontline buys tanker fleet.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-08-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish shipping company Frontline AB said it agreed at a board meeting on Wednesday to buy six tanker vessels -- five VLCC's built between 1991 and 1993 and a Suezmax -- from its main shareholder Hemen Holding B.V.</p>
<p>Frontline also agreed with its owners to buy two store OBO vessels, Front Climber and Front Leader. The two ships are sister vessels to Frontline's own fleet of six OBO vessels.</p>
<p>The total purchase cost was around 3.0 billion crowns, Frontline said in a statement.  </p>
<p>Frontline said it will pay for the vessels through a share issue to the ship's owners.</p>
<p>-- Simon Haydon, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
